@* Three variants, and the difference is the ground each sits on: nothing, a border, or a muted
   fill. A list of rows usually wants the first and one separator. *@
<div class="flex w-[420px] flex-col gap-3">
    <Item><ItemContent><ItemTitle>Default</ItemTitle>
        <ItemDescription>No ground of its own.</ItemDescription></ItemContent></Item>
    <Item Variant="outline"><ItemContent><ItemTitle>Outline</ItemTitle>
        <ItemDescription>A border, for a row that stands alone.</ItemDescription></ItemContent></Item>
    <Item Variant="muted"><ItemContent><ItemTitle>Muted</ItemTitle>
        <ItemDescription>Filled, for a row that is one of several.</ItemDescription></ItemContent></Item>
</div>
